[bxb@lanl.gov (barry j. berenberg) suggests:]
>   Nethack should allow some way for characters to make their own traps.
>   Here's what may be a ... solution:  wands aimed at the ground (>)
>   create a trap.  These traps can either be permanent or of a finite
>   duration.  Whether the wand is blessed/uncursed/cursed makes a
>   difference:
.
interesting ... i'd suggest that only blessed wands be able to do this
and that the effect wouldn't take place until after the character steps
off and then back on the trap. uncursed and cursed wands would behave
as they do now.
.
>   Most wands create a trap which behaves just like the wand, but a few
.
i'll only highlight my exceptions ...
.
>	   WAND			TRAP
	   magic missile	magic missile (permanent)
	   cancellation		cancellation (you once, monsters always)
	   create monster	create monster (you once, monsters always)
	   nothing		no trap is created
	   probing		enlightenment (you once)
	   opening		remove curse (you once)
	   locking		create curse (you once)
	   wishing		any trap of your choice (including nothing)
	   teleportation	teleportation (perm)

i'd also suggest that the trap names really correspond to the wand names
(i.e. an opening trap would have the effect of removing curses) so you
only have to learn the names of the wands. trapdoors would be an exception.
you should be able to remember the location of the traps in your floor map
after you walk away (even in unlit areas)! sounds like fun!! 3.1 has the
potential to be singularly incredible ...

